        "falseColor": true,
        "notes": "A small region from Cassini’s 11 June 2004 flyby, supported by 41 original VIMS pixels. False color assigns red to about 2.02 µm, green to 1.59 µm and blue to 1.28 µm. All three channels share a 0–0.03 I/F display range and gamma 2.2; this stretch changes the display only. No photometric correction is applied, so illumination remains. Archive noise filtering and local replacement are retained; original detector defects and potentially affected neighbors are excluded. Gray grid marks unsupported areas and scan gaps. Placement is coarse on the existing shape, with several-kilometer spatial uncertainty. Fine surface positions are not established.",
