          "image": "/scenes/phoebe/phoebe-ice-absorption-legend.webp"
        },
        "notes": "Near-2.02 µm water-ice band depth relative to a linear 1.82–2.20 µm continuum, using 41 original VIMS pixels from one small region in Cassini’s 11 June 2004 flyby. This measures absorption strength, not ice abundance. Viewing angle, grain size and noise also affect the values; no photometric correction is applied. Archive noise filtering and local replacement remain; original detector defects and potentially affected neighbors are excluded. Display colors saturate outside 0.1–0.3; original numerical values are retained. Gray grid marks unsupported areas and scan gaps. The region is placed coarsely on the existing shape, with several-kilometer spatial uncertainty.",
